.TH SATER-MAP 1 "October 2026" "SATER Map" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sater-map \- direction finding map for distress beacon searches (SATER)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sater-map
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sater-map
draws on a map the bearings several stations take on a distress beacon,
each with its uncertainty cone, and computes the zone where they cross: its
centre in decimal degrees, degrees-minutes-seconds and MGRS, its radius and
surface. A station heard at S0 stays on the map without a bearing.
.PP
The best estimate is the least-squares position of all the bearings, each
weighted by its uncertainty, with its 50 % and 95 % confidence ellipses and a
check that the bearings agree. A bearing read on a compass (magnetic north)
is corrected by the declination of the World Magnetic Model (WMM2025).
.PP
Bearings travel by APRS as standard DF reports: a field team sends its own,
the command post receives those of the operation's callsigns over APRS-IS or
a KISS TNC on TCP (Dire Wolf, Soundmodem) and puts them on the map. Each
SSID of a callsign is a station of its own. The bearing of a station without
APRS, read out by telephone, is sent for it as an APRS object named after
it. The Android application sends by radio through a modem of its own (Dire
Wolf, built in) and an audio interface.
.PP
The mission timer, the history of the recorded bearings, the kilometres each
station drove and the position of the beacon make up the mission, which is
saved as it changes and restored at the next start. It is exported as a PDF
report, KML, JSON (the format of SATER Map 2) or a stand-alone HTML map.
.PP
Map tiles come from OpenStreetMap, OpenTopoMap, IGN or Esri. "Download
visible tiles" stores the current view, two zoom levels below and above, for
use without a network ("Offline").
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/SATER_Map/station_presets.json
The station presets.
.TP
.I ~/.config/SATER_Map/autosave.json
The current mission.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/SATER_Map/tiles/
The downloaded tiles, \fIprovider\fR/\fIz\fR/\fIx\fR/\fIy\fR.png (another
folder can be chosen in the preferences).
.TP
.I ~/.config/SATER_Map/SATER_Map.conf
The settings.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SATER_MAP_RASTER=1
Draw the map on the CPU even when OpenGL is available.
.TP
.B SATER_SCREENSHOT_DIR=\fIdir\fR
Render the interface with a sample mission into PNG files in \fIdir\fR and quit.
